    "markdown": "# Warning-only API (v1)\n\nNothing here is broken enough to fail a build — which is exactly what\n--strict is for.\n\n**Base URL:** `http://localhost/api`\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [soft](#soft)\n\n## soft\n\n### An unknown type is a warning: the generator carries on and calls it a\nstring, so the spec is wrong but nothing is broken.\n\n`POST /v1/soft/unknownType`\n\n**Request Body:**\n\nContent-Type: `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\n|-------|------|----------|-------------|\n| `when` | string | Yes | When |\n\n**Responses:**\n\n- `200` — Response payload\n\n---\n",
    "curl": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Warning-only API (v1) — cURL examples\n# Auto-generated from OpenAPI spec. Do not edit manually.\n\nBASE_URL=\"http://localhost/api\"\nTOKEN=\"${API_TOKEN:-}\"\n\n# An unknown type is a warning: the generator carries on and calls it a\nstring, so the spec is wrong but nothing is broken.\ncurl -s -X POST \\\n  -d \"when=\" \\\n  \"${BASE_URL}/v1/soft/unknownType\"\n",
